A||||10||Wolfhound||Ferrari 335 Spyder rebody||||14||
Z||000000||Wolfhound||03-18-2001||09:02 AM||||I heard a rumor that an old friend of mine's son was building a Ferrari kit car. I went to see what the story was .<BR> It turns out that it,s a Fiero based 335 Spyder. He is using a 85 GT as the base. The project is coming along nicely.<BR> After looking it over I asked the majic question.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> What happened to the body parts you pulled off the frame? Now I have to drive over there and pick them up this afternoon along with the interior parts and sunroof. <BR> Yes I will take my Sony digital camera and post back here with more info!<BR>  <BR>||||reg||14
Z||000001||Spyder||03-18-2001||11:32 AM||||Wolfhound send me the pics of his progress!<BR>Also where is he located at?||||reg||14
Z||000002||Wolfhound||03-18-2001||12:19 PM||||Spyder, His shop and the car are located in Auburn Alabama, but he lives in Montgomery.<BR>I,m going over this afternoon around 2:00PM and I,ll post pics here when I get back. I,ll get a phone number and if he is on line an email address while there. I will be checking on it as it progresses, at this point the body is on the frame.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||03-18-2001||07:13 PM||||OK! here are a few photos of the car.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spyder1.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spyder2.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spyder3.JPG"> <BR>And another pretty machine that lives in the shop.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/alexbike.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Spyder||03-19-2001||02:13 AM||||Cool,<BR>Thanks for the pics,<BR>Keep us posted on his progress.<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000005||THE BEAST||03-19-2001||03:09 PM||||From who did he got he's Kit? <P>and, How much?||||reg||7
Z||000006||Wolfhound||03-20-2001||05:31 AM||||Beast, He told me the name but it escapes me right now. It was out of California. The body panels are really high quality. The finish is excellent. He mentioned you could get them for about 3500 but this kit was taken from the actual car and was about 5500. I,ll get the name for you in the next few days.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Songman||03-20-2001||11:30 PM||||Supposedly, the only kit that was taken from the actual car was the one that was used to build the stunt cars in the movie, The Rock. That company fell under the Ferrari axe. Could be that he got some old stock from that company that was left over.<P>And by looking at the pictures, I believe that could be the case. One mistake that most 355 kits make are the lower air intakes beneath the doors. On the Ferrari they are part of the rocker panel and do not open with the door. On most kits including this one, they are made as part of the door and there is no visible rocker panel. There are a few kits out there now that have the correct rocker setup. But only until Ferrari finds them. I have a buddy up in NY that is doing them. He switched from 328s to 355s last year.<P>The 355 kits are murder to put together. Even with the best kits! Nothing ever lines up and there is a lot of fabrication. But we all still love them, don't we? I know I do.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Wolfhound||03-21-2001||04:47 AM||||Songman, I believe you are right about its origin. He mentioned the Farrari had closed down the company and there were few kits left.<BR> The body panels are hand laid not chopper gunned. He mentioned that it came with a crappy vidio that showed how to hack it together and was totally usless. No written instructions at all. His dad is an excellent engineer so it will get done right.<BR>The engine compartment and cradle are stretched 4 inches. I,ll have more info by the end of the week.||||reg||1
Z||000009||mshill||03-21-2001||03:24 PM||||Wolfhound,  I have decided that the ferrari kits are brutal to put together as well.  My F50 is much more work than I expected.  I even took 3 weeks off in February to work on it and have not made too much progress.  My instructions consisted of a one page sheet with a couple of very good drawings and generally useless info like "lower/tilt radiator 4 inches" and "screw rocker panel to frame"...  I am a fairly adept engineer and will finish this car this summer, but it is sometimes very frustrating.||||reg||1
Z||000010||SWTKSTMS||03-22-2001||04:42 PM||||MSHILL. I WOULD LOVE TO SEE THAT WHEN YOU GET IT DONE.||||reg||1
